Map shell
=========

The page shell, dialog, canvas (pan, zoom, drag) and the "sdlc" layout in this
folder come from super-board by EricTechPro (MIT licence):

  https://github.com/EricTechPro/super-board
  commit d0b7d5a6850614ca809477c1af43d5d7da408726
  files:  diagrams/_shared/ shell.css shell.html shell.js skillmap.css
          skillmap.js canvas.js layout_sdlc.py layout_sdlc.js README.md
  licence: LICENSE in this folder (copied from the super-board repo root)

These nine files are copied unchanged. The licence text is in LICENSE.

Written for this site (not from super-board)
--------------------------------------------

  build.py      A short build script. It follows super-board's
                build_skillmap.py, but takes one map.json and writes one
                HTML file. It swaps the super-board site nav for a link bar
                for this site, reads the site's day/night choice
                (localStorage key "theme"), and adds status badges and a key.
  platforms.py  A stub. layout_sdlc.py imports it for tool logos. This site
                shows no tool logos, so the stub returns nothing.

Build
-----

  python3 -I maps/_shared/build.py maps/src/skills/map.json maps/skills.html
  python3 -I maps/_shared/build.py maps/src/flow/map.json   maps/flow.html

The built pages are single files. They load no library and no outside file.
